  "ruleText": "Saf-C 603.02 Application of Federal Regulations.\n\n(a) The federal agencies and titles referred to in the federal regulations incorporated by Saf-C 603.01 shall be construed as follows:\n\n(1) United States Department of Transportation and any other federal agency where there is no comparable state agency also means the New Hampshire department of safety; and\n\n(2) Secretary of Transportation and any other federal title also means commissioner of the New Hampshire department of safety.\n\n(b) Notwithstanding any rule to the contrary, in the event these rules conflict with a federal regulation incorporated by Saf-C 603.01, the federal regulation shall take precedence.\n\nSource. #1461 eff. 10-16-79; ss by #2249, eff 12-31-82; ss by #2945, eff 1-3-85, EXPIRED: 1-3-91\n\nNew. #5219, eff 9-4-91; ss by #6562, Interim, eff 9-4-97, EXPIRES: 1-2-98; ss by #6615, eff 10-25-97, EXPIRED:10-25-05\n\nNew. #8507, INTERIM, eff 12-7-05, EXPIRED: 6-5-06\n\nNew. #8721-B, eff 9-8-06 (formerly Saf-C 601.04), EXPIRED: 9-8-14\n\nNew. #12373, INTERIM, eff 8-31-17, EXPIRED: 2-27-18\n\nNew. #12516, eff 4-23-18",
